 'fix/stft-huge-nfft': ['Reject data shorter than nfft in stft before planning the FFT', `## Summary
- \`stft\` planned the FFT and allocated \`nfft/2+1\` bins before checking that one window fits, so \`stft(&[0.0; 4], 1 << 40, 0)\` aborted the process ("memory allocation of 3758096384 bytes failed"), which can't be caught.
- It now returns \`MusicError::DataShorterThanWindow\` before planning anything, so memory is bounded by the input size. Parameter errors (\`InvalidNfft\`, \`InvalidOverlap\`) still come first.
- **Behaviour change:** data shorter than \`nfft\` used to give \`nfft/2+1\` empty bins and is now an error. The internal callers already check this first.

## Tests
- \`stft_rejects_data_shorter_than_window\` (unit test) and \`stft_errors\` in \`tests/errors_test.rs\`.
- \`cargo fmt --check\`, \`cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings\` and \`cargo test -- --include-ignored\` pass.`],
 'fix/ifb-memory': ['Build IFB covariances one bin at a time; count each bin once', `## Summary
- \`ifb_music_spectrum\` held every active bin's \`n_mics × n_mics\` cross-spectral matrix at once, roughly \`n_mics² × nfft/2 × 16\` bytes. Each matrix is now built inside the per-bin loop, so only one exists at a time. The spectra are bit-for-bit identical.
- Duplicate entries in \`bins\` were each counted in the geometric mean, which silently weighted them. Bins are now sorted and deduplicated, and this is documented.

## Tests
- \`ifb_duplicate_and_reordered_bins_are_ignored\` checks with exact equality that \`[36, 14, 14, 36, 36]\` gives the same spectrum as \`[14, 36]\`.
- The golden, ifb and broadband tests pin the refactor.
- \`cargo fmt --check\`, \`cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings\` and \`cargo test -- --include-ignored\` pass.`],
 'fix/zero-sources': ['Reject zero sources with MusicError::NoSources', `## Summary
- With \`n_sources = 0\`, \`estimate_doa\` and \`estimate_doa_from_real\` returned \`Ok(vec![])\`, and \`ifb_music_spectrum\` and \`noise_subspace\` used the whole space as the "noise subspace".
- The new \`MusicError::NoSources\` is returned from the shared \`check_sources\`, so every entry point that takes \`n_sources\` rejects 0. \`TooManySources\` is still checked first.
- **API change:** a new public enum variant.

## Tests
- Zero-sources cases in \`tests/errors_test.rs\` for all four functions, plus the Display message.
- \`degenerate_configurations_find_nothing\` now expects \`NoSources\`.
- \`cargo fmt --check\`, \`cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings\` and \`cargo test -- --include-ignored\` pass.`],
 'fix/select-bins-scale': ['Normalise the data in select_bins_by_energy', `## Summary
- \`select_bins_by_energy\` was the only data entry point that didn't call \`normalised_real\`, so its STFT power sums underflowed or overflowed. A 1 kHz tone scaled by 1e-170 gave \`Err(SilentData)\`, and scaled by 1e300 it selected all 80 bins instead of bin 10.
- It now divides by the same power of two as the other entry points. That division is exact, so results at normal scales don't change.

## Tests
- \`select_bins_by_energy_does_not_depend_on_scale\` checks scales from 1e-300 to 1e300, a two-tone case, and that DC-only data is still silent.
- \`cargo fmt --check\`, \`cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings\` and \`cargo test -- --include-ignored\` pass.`],
};
